{"nodes": [{"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_backend_contract_answers", "label": "GEMS QCF Backend Contract Answers", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_gems_server_group_identification", "label": "GEMS identification via qcf_library.server_groups", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": "Section A", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stored per QCF row and copied from the RFQ at insertBulkQcf time rather than derived at read time, so it is stable; but nothing prevents a mixed-group QCF and no code checks for one."}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_cl_approved_at_signal", "label": "cl_approved_at as the authoritative post-CL signal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": "Section B", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "qcf_approved=1 means 'PO published' (set only after syncAutoPO succeeds) and cannot distinguish who approved, so the frontend must key on cl_approved_at instead."}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_capability_fields_contract", "label": "Role-aware capability fields (canApprove, canManualSourcing)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": "Section C", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returning booleans rather than raw serverGroups plus clApprovedAt keeps the GEMS rule from being reimplemented in two codebases; it changes canApprove semantics from per-endpoint to per-authenticated-role."}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_management_approval_security_gap", "label": "Management QCF approval eligibility gap", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": "Section D1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The update predicate checks only qcf_number and null approval fields, so Management can approve a GEMS QCF before or after CL and trigger Auto PO; fix is 403 for policy denial and 409 for state conflicts."}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_manual_sourcing_role_guard_gap", "label": "Manual Sourcing endpoint has no role or state guard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": "Section D2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The iSourcing board mutation runs before RFQ/QCF status updates, so a late rejection would orphan a board card; validation must happen before any mutation, and the client-supplied is_system_action flag is not a security boundary."}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_cs_token_access", "label": "CS token access to QCF detail", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": "Section E", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "QCF tokens are entirely unbound - the payload carries only qcf_number/rfq_number/vendor_code and the middleware verifies signature and expiry without consulting qcf_token_email, so a revoked token still works; this answer was later reversed by planning decision 2."}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_gems_manual_po_recipients", "label": "GEMS Manual PO email recipients (categoryMatrixResolver)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": "Section F", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Main CS and all Sub CS go in To (the data model draws no access-rights distinction between them) with the approving CL in Cc; the existing buildCsRecipients puts Subs in Cc and is unused, so a new resolver is added rather than repurposing it."}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_qcf_sub_category_id_blocker", "label": "qcf_library.sub_category_id lineage blocker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": "Section E2/F2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "category_matrices is keyed on category_id but qcf_library has no sub_category_id column, so CS PIC resolution has no join key; the lineage qcf_library.rfq_item_id to rfq_library.id to rfq_library.sub_category_id must be materialized first."}], "edges": [{"source": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_backend_contract_answers", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_gems_server_group_identification", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": "Section A", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_backend_contract_answers", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_cl_approved_at_signal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen